    <system:String x:Key="Guide_ProfileGuideTitle">Profile Guide:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_ProfileGuide1">Set profile settings such as width, height, background color and typography defaults and save them.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_ProfileGuide2">Mouse over icons to see more details.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_ProfileGuide3">Direct 2D Acceleration uses your GPU instead of CPU for faster frame rendering up to 100 FPS. It also uses VRAM instead of memory to load images and GIFs. This results in faster GIF rendering and lower CPU usage for use cases with larger panel sizes and multiple high quality/high framerate images and GIFs.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_ProfileGuideDirect2DNote">Direct2D is only available for HDMI/DP displays. Enabling for USB panels will not have an impact. USB displays are mostly limited by their update bus.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Direct2DNotesTitle">Direct2D Acceleration Notes:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Direct2DNote1">Direct2D uses a different rendering engine. This results in different fonts being displayed differently when it is on versus off. This means that text may appear smaller or larger, and be offset lower, higher or more towards the left or right.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Direct2DNote2">Adjust Font Scale, Text X Offset and Text Y Offset accordingly for backward compatibility with Non-Direct2D profiles.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_Direct2DNote3">Panel FPS shows the rendering speed of that particular panel. Although it uses mostly GPU, a CPU bottleneck by other non-Direct2D profiles or external applications can impact the speed as it is capped by the sensor calculations. The maximum FPS is 100.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AdditionalNotesTitle">Additional Notes:</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AdditionalNote1">This software is provided on a best effort basis. Expect bugs and/or crashes. You are encouraged to save often.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AdditionalNote2">Performance and memory usage is largely determined by the number of active profiles and size of your panel and number of images and GIFs.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_AdditionalNote3">Join our discord for support, feature requests and share your designs by using the export button to generate an .infopanel file for uploading.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Guide_RememberSaveWork">Lastly, remember to save your work. Updates are live but not auto saved.</system:String>
